<title>AUSTRIA: Boehler sells real estate to Gerling.</title>
<headline>Boehler sells real estate to Gerling.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian high-grade steelmaker Boehler-Uddeholm AG said on Friday it had sold off real estate in the German cities of Duesseldorf and Neuss to German insurer Gerling Konzern Allgemeine Versicherungs-AG.</p>
<p>Boehler said the deal encompassing 974 apartments brought a book profit of around 200 million schillings.</p>
<p>The company said the move was in line with its strategy of selling off its peripheral businesses in order to focus on its core businesses in the steel industry.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12 254</p>
